  "issue": {
    "headline": "A city that owns its power company, on a shrinking aquifer",
    "body": "Lubbock runs a municipal electric utility and sits on the Ogallala. Industrial load growth — including data-centre-scale load — lands on ratepayers through the utility rather than through the tax roll, which means the decision that raises a household bill is made in a utility board packet, not in a budget hearing.",
    "record": "Lubbock Power & Light board agendas and rate ordinances, and the City's water supply and wholesale-power contracts."
  },
